\end_inset

.
 Let us consider the market for good 1.
 By the market clearing condition, we have
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
\frac{8-4p}{p+4}+\frac{14p+2}{3p+1} & = & 4\\
\frac{(4-2p)(3p+1)+(7p+1)(p+4)}{(p+4)(3p+1)} & = & 2\\
7p^{2}+13p & = & 0\\
p(7p+13) & = & 0\\
p & \in & \left\{ 0,-\frac{13}{7}\right\} 
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

Neither of the two solutions for 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 fall in the required range.
 Thus, a competitive equilibrium fails to exist in this case.
